  "notes": "Nasdaq's 2025 Sustainability Report publishes a country-by-country tax transparency table (GRI 207-4) with employees, third-party revenue, profit before tax and cash corporate income tax for 38 countries; employees and tax paid are recorded here (revenue and profit by country are in the same table but are not repeated). Georgia, listed in the 2024 table, is not in the 2025 table and its row was removed. A value of 0 means the table prints 0 (amounts are rounded to $ millions). The 10-K's 9,525 headcount at Dec 31, 2025 includes part-time staff and non-wholly owned subsidiaries, so it differs from the 9,506 in the sustainability report. The report also has a Workforce by Gender and Country table (countries with over 50 employees). No state-level data is published. Nasdaq owns no real property (FY2025 10-K Item 2).",
